        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/12.1b.html">12.1b</a></td><td>Grid/Symmetry Jam: Build Day 1</td><td>the board as data; bounds; one move</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/12.1c.html">12.1c</a></td><td>Grid/Symmetry Jam: Build Day 2</td><td>rules engines, mirrored opponents, the render sign</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/12.1d.html">12.1d</a></td><td>Grid/Symmetry Jam: Playtest</td><td>grid-specific tells; death coordinates</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/12.1e.html">12.1e</a></td><td>Grid/Symmetry Jam: Showcase</td><td>star votes and the constraint's receipt</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/12.2a.html">12.2a</a></td><td>Placeholder Jam: Day 1 (topic TBA)</td><td>topic-on-time or the flex menu</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/12.2b.html">12.2b</a></td><td>Placeholder Jam: Day 2 + Year Retro</td><td>ship, then write to September-you</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Concepts this unit owns</h2>
<p>The grid is a <strong>list of lists</strong> (Unit 10's data structure, two-dimensional) and the year's last word on constraints. The final retro — pattern inventory, September letter — is the course's real final exam. CED: AAP-3, CRD-1, IOC-1.</p>

